menu "Station: NTRIP casters"

    config NTRIP_MAX_CASTERS
        int "Maximum caster slots"
        range 1 8
        default 4
        help
            Number of casters the station can stream to at once (Onocoy plus
            others). Each slot costs one task (created once at boot), one
            socket and, with TLS, tens of KB of PSRAM for the session.

    config NTRIP_TASK_PRIO
        int "Caster task priority"
        range 2 20
        default 8

    config NTRIP_TASK_STACK
        int "Caster task stack (bytes)"
        range 3072 16384
        default 8192

    config NTRIP_TCP_CONNECT_TIMEOUT_MS
        int "TCP connect timeout for plain slots (ms)"
        range 2000 30000
        default 5000

    config NTRIP_CONNECT_TIMEOUT_MS
        int "TLS slots: connect and handshake timeout (ms)"
        range 2000 60000
        default 10000
        help
            TLS slots: esp_tls timeout_ms. It bounds the connect and each
            handshake wait, so the handshake can take up to about twice
            this.

    config NTRIP_SEND_TIMEOUT_MS
        int "Socket send/receive timeout (ms)"
        range 1000 60000
        default 10000
        help
            A caster whose TCP window stays full this long is dropped and
            reconnected; the hub's lag limit keeps it from falling behind
            meanwhile.

    config NTRIP_CONNECT_BUDGET_S
        int "Longest a slot may stay CONNECTING (s)"
        range 20 300
        default 60
        help
            Covers DNS, connect, TLS and the caster's reply. The health
            monitor restarts a slot that overruns it (only that slot).

    config NTRIP_PROTECTED_MAX_BACKOFF_S
        int "Longest transient reconnect backoff for the protected (Onocoy) slot (s)"
        range 5 120
        default 30
        help
            Transient failures (network, timeouts, caster restarts) of the
            protected slot back off to 15 s, and to this cap after 10 min of
            continuous failure. Every second offline counts against the
            daily streak budget.

    config NTRIP_AUTH_TRANSIENT_WINDOW_S
        int "Treat rejections as transient for this long after a disconnect or boot (s)"
        range 60 1800
        default 300
        help
            Casters may still hold the previous session for a while after a
            reconnect and reply with an error that looks like a bad password.
            Within this window such a rejection, on credentials that worked
            before, follows the slot profile's "mountpoint busy" delays.

    config NTRIP_SOURCE_STALL_S
        int "Close a slot's session after this long without RTCM (s)"
        range 5 60
        default 10
        help
            Casters drop or count as bad a source that stays connected but
            silent (some after about 10-16 s). A pause for receiver work is
            a planned stall with the same limit.

    config NTRIP_PROTECTED_SOURCE_STALL_S
        int "Same for the protected (Onocoy) slot (s)"
        range 10 300
        default 60
        help
            Staying connected through a short stall costs the Onocoy streak
            less than reconnecting, if the caster keeps the silent session.
            PROVISIONAL, to be confirmed against the caster's idle timeout.

endmenu
